 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Initiates complex N-linked carbohydrate formation.Essential for the conversion of high-mannose to hybrid and complexN-glycans. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:1702225}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=N(4)-(alpha-D-Man-(1-&gt;3)-[alpha-D-Man-(1-&gt;3)-[alpha-D-Man-(1-&gt;6)]-alpha-D-Man-(1-&gt;6)]-beta-D-Man-(1-&gt;4)-beta-D-GlcNAc-(1-&gt;4)-beta-D-GlcNAc)-L-asparaginyl-[protein] (isomer 5A1,2) +UDP-N-acetyl-alpha-D-glucosamine = H(+) + N(4)-{beta-D-GlcNAc-(1-&gt;2)-alpha-D-Man-(1-&gt;3)-[alpha-D-Man-(1-&gt;3)-[alpha-D-Man-(1-&gt;6)]-alpha-D-Man-(1-&gt;6)]-beta-D-Man-(1-&gt;4)-beta-D-GlcNAc-(1-&gt;4)-beta-D-GlcNAc}-L-asparaginyl-[protein] + UDP;Xref=Rhea:RHEA:11456, Rhea:RHEA-COMP:14367, Rhea:RHEA-COMP:14368, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378, ChEBI:CHEBI:57705,ChEBI:CHEBI:58223, ChEBI:CHEBI:59087, ChEBI:CHEBI:60625;EC=2.4.1.101; Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:1702225};COFACTOR:Name=Mn(2+); Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:29035;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:1702225};Note=The cofactor is mostly bound to the substrate.{ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P27115};PATHWAY: Protein modification; protein glycosylation.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:1702225}.SUBUNIT: Interacts with MGAT4D. {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P27808}.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Golgi apparatus membrane{ECO:0000269|PubMed:20378551}; Single-pass type II membraneprotein {ECO:0000305}.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the glycosyltransferase 13 family.{ECO:0000305}.WEB RESOURCE: Name=Functional Glycomics Gateway - GTase;Note=Alpha-1,3-mannosyl-glycoprotein 2-beta-N-acetylglucosaminyltransferase;URL=&quot;http://www.functionalglycomics.org/glycomics/molecule/jsp/glycoEnzyme/viewGlycoEnzyme.jsp?gbpId=gt_hum_535&quot;; COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
