 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://www.ctdbase.org/#ref_protein_gene_55650</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Alpha-1,6-mannosyltransferase involved inglycosylphosphatidylinositol-anchor biosynthesis. Transfers thesecond mannose to the glycosylphosphatidylinositol during GPIprecursor assembly. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:15623507,ECO:0000269|PubMed:15720390}.PATHWAY: Glycolipid biosynthesis; glycosylphosphatidylinositol-anchor biosynthesis. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:15623507}.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Endoplasmic reticulum membrane{ECO:0000269|PubMed:15623507}; Multi-pass membrane protein{ECO:0000269|PubMed:15623507}.PTM: Not N-glycosylated. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:15623507}.DISEASE: Hyperphosphatasia with mental retardation syndrome 1(HPMRS1) [MIM:239300]: A severe syndrome characterized by elevatedserum alkaline phosphatase, severe mental retardation, seizures,hypotonia, facial dysmorphism, and hypoplastic terminal phalanges.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:20802478}. Note=The disease is caused bymutations affecting the gene represented in this entry.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the PIGV family. {ECO:0000305}. COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">PIGV_HUMAN Reviewed; 493 AA.</bp:comment>
